statement:
A security gate reads a line of text off a badge scanner and the badge reader notices that a suspicious number of badges look the same from both directions.

You are given one line of text. Decide whether it is a palindrome, where:

- comparison ignores the case of letters;
- every character that is neither an ASCII letter nor an ASCII digit is treated as if it were not there at all;
- after both rules are applied, the remaining sequence must equal its own reverse.

A line may therefore become empty or a single character after cleaning, and both cases are palindromes.

